{
 "name": "thesis_reads",
 "_comment": [
  "THE thesis read campaign (2026-10-24), meant for a dedicated cloud machine.",
  "Point reads: v100 (4M x 100 B) and v16 (20M x 16 B), scrambled zipf (hot records scattered) and raw",
  "zipf (hot keys contiguous, the paper's), 0.9.  SUTs: stock; bf (reference defaults: record mode);",
  "bf_nofull (M2 ablation: no full-page copies); bf read_record_cache=0 (reference page mode);",
  "bf adaptive_full=8 (X1, our experiment, default off).  Scans: 32-row, stock / bf / bf_noscan (M3",
  "ablation) / bf_nofull.  Mix: read 90 / scan 10, stock / bf / bf scan_promotion=0.",
  "32 MiB budget, direct I/O (the reference's I/O model).  QUOTE device reads/op (dio.reads/op) first;",
  "throughput second, and only from a quiet machine.  Report cached_records and evictions beside hit rates.",
  "ADDED 2026-10-24, from the cost model (costmodel.py) and the X1 question:",
  "  * budget sweep (v100, stock vs bf, 8M and 128M beside the main 32M cells): the model predicts the",
  "    scrambled win GROWS with budget (1.40x / 1.57x / 1.87x) and the raw loss deepens (0.96x / 0.89x / 0.73x)",
  "    for a pure record cache -- predicted before measured.  Warmup scales with the budget so the ring fills.",
  "  * X1 adaptive_full N = 4 / 16 beside the main N = 8 (raw cells; N = 4 also on v100 scrambled, the risk side).",
  "  * bf_cap1k: the mini-page cap at 1024 instead of 2048 (the reference's max_mini_page_size), i.e. leaves go",
  "    full EARLIER with no adaptivity -- the static baseline X1 must beat on raw without the cost on scrambled."
 ],
 "datasets": {
  "v100": {
   "records": 4000000,
   "value_len": 100,
   "key_spacing": 16
  },
  "v16": {
   "records": 20000000,
   "value_len": 16,
   "key_spacing": 16
  }
 },
